UID:124310-1794661200-1794664800@www.naturalsciences.org
SUMMARY:The Comeback of Blue-Throated Macaws
DESCRIPTION:20 years of conservation success: the comeback of blue-throated macaws\n \nJoin us along with the Wake Audubon Society in the SECU Daily Planet Theater for a special presentation with Dorothy Paterson\, executive director for Bird Endowment. \nMs. Dorothy Paterson\, the President & Executive Director of Bird Endowment\, will join us via Zoom to deliver “Twenty Years of Conservation Success: The Comeback of Blue-Throated Macaws” inside the SECU Daily Planet Theater. \nBlue-Throated Macaws are a critically endangered parrot native exclusively to the Beni Savannas of north-central Bolivia. Only 300-500 individuals remain in the wild. Their severe decline is driven by habitat loss\, the illegal pet trade\, and the historic use of its feathers in traditional dances.
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/the-comeback-of-blue-throated-macaws/
LOCATION:Nature Research Center\, 121 West Jones Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adults,Educators,General Events,Lectures,SECU Daily Planet Theater,Teens
ORGANIZER;CN="Chris%20Smith":MAILTO:christopher.smith@naturalsciences.org
GEO:35.7822405;-78.6409677
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Nature Research Center 121 West Jones Street Raleigh NC 27601 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=121 West Jones Street:geo:-78.6409677,35.7822405
END:VEVENT
