SUMMARY:Tree Camp
DESCRIPTION:All programs at Prairie Ridge currently require pre-registration. Register for this program for ages 18+\nGet a hands-on introduction to tree identification in this dendrology crash course! We will explore the Jesse P. Perry III Arboretum at Prairie Ridge to learn how to recognize common Piedmont trees using leaves\, twigs\, bark\, seeds and simple identification keys. In addition we will learn about species growing in the arboretum that are more common to the mountains or the coast. You’ll also discover how to contribute to collaborative science by tracking seasonal life cycles with Nature’s Notebook. 
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/tree-camp/
LOCATION:Prairie Ridge\, 1671 Gold Star Drive\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27607\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adults,Collaborative Science,Outdoor Experiences
ORGANIZER;CN="Julie%20Hall":MAILTO:julie.hall@naturalsciences.org
GEO:35.812182885871;-78.713963528554
